@tradition rec-wso
// W3 (rec writer; lead 18: fields from plans/rec-traditions-plan.html FINAL and the brief; RA owns the format).
// Winner Stays On: Sundays 11:30-16:30 from Day 7, the Lightdisc court and stands. Pell keeps the chalkboard and rings a
// hand bell for each new game; tap the gate to play next (RA's recTap). FOR RA: skip the Lightdisc Cup's Sundays (days 28,
// 56, ...: the Cup takes this slot; the format has no 'except', so the Cup's prio is higher). The stands are a gathering
// (exempt from the deck's cap). Intended who: disc-player (RA's new habit) 90% once it exists.
k: 486
title: Winner Stays On
when: weekly sunday from day 7
at: 11:30-16:30
min: 30
prio: 0
jitter: 60
where: 7 room Stands: rec:seat
hold: none
who: pell always, juniors 40%, works 35%, everyone 25%
anim: everyone talk
host: pell
from: pell
flag: rec.on

== mail
- Winner Stays On tomorrow, {time} at the Lightdisc court. Pell's chalkboard by the gate: write your name, wait your turn, win and stay on. Sandwiches from the grab shelf.

== ask
- Winner Stays On today. I'm putting my name on the board. Low down. Very modest.   #funny
- Coming to the court later? Pell's been on since half eleven. Somebody has to stop him.   #funny
- Lightdisc this afternoon. Even if you just watch, the stands are the best seats aboard.

== here
- Next! Name on the board, wait for the bell.
- Oh, that curve! Did you see that curve?
- Winner stays on. Loser gets a sandwich. Everyone wins, really.   #funny
- Shh, it's a long rally. Don't jinx it.

== thanks
- You find a spot in the stands. Pell rings the hand bell, two more step up, and the disc starts to fly.

== chatter
- Three wins in a row and your name goes on the foyer board. Pell's on it four times.   #funny
- I lasted two games at Winner Stays On. Two! A personal best.   #funny
- Who was on longest on Sunday? Pell. It's always Pell.
- The stands get loud on a Sunday. Bring your voice.
